## FengChaoSkills Business Memory

Start new project conversations from `fengwang/FENGWANG.md`, then route through `fengwang/memory-map.md` to the smallest relevant context set.

Project-local FengChao skill is available at `.claude/skills/fengchao-business-memory/SKILL.md`. When FengChaoSkills applies, read that file and follow it.

Use task/changelog maintenance only after a real development task has landed project changes. Plan mode captures only `plan-records/`; durable user business explanations capture only `conversation-records/`. Plans and conversations do not update `business-context/` by default.

Before the final response for a completed development task:

1. Extract the user's true business intent, final delivered solution, key decisions, implementation evidence, and validation.
2. Create an immutable `task-records/YYYY-MM-DD_NNN_title.md`.
3. Create `changelog/YYYY-MM-DD_NNN_title.md`.
4. Update `task-records/TASK-INDEX.md` and `changelog/CHANGELOG-INDEX.md`.
5. If stable business behavior changed, update the relevant `business-context/` domain pages.
6. Update `fengwang/memory-map.md`.
7. Run `fengchao check`, or the equivalent command configured by the project.
<!-- FENGCHAO-BUSINESS-MEMORY:END -->
